  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?",
  "worked_solution": "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096470/assets/bf2098a7fcdecce8405dadf6f9cd2c78da19d1c0a7ae2c9c9e95a897a64ef9d9.png)",
